      <div type="clause" n="77">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 77</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="77" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="88" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon oðrum ða geweald forslea uppe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.1"/> on þam sweoran ⁊ forwundie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.2"/> to þam swiðe, þæt he nage þære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.3"/> geweald, ⁊ hwæðre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.4"/> lifie swa gescended<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.5"/>, geselle him mon C<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.5"/> scill. to bote, buton him witan ryhtre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.6"/> ⁊ mare gereccan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="77" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="88" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.1-2"/> oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ða geweald forslea up<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.2-2"/> on ðam sweoran ⁊ forwundige to þam swiðe, þæt he nage ðæra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.3-2"/> geweald, ⁊ hwæðre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.4-2"/> libbe swa gescynded<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.5-2"/> him C scll' to bote, buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.1-2"/> him witon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.1-2"/> mare gereccan ⁊ ryhtre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="77" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="89" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf man oðrum ða gewald forsléa uppe on ðam sweore ⁊ forwundie to ðam swiðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he nage þær geweald, ⁊ ðeahhwæðere lifige swa g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>scend, gesylle him mon hund scill' to bote, buton him witan rihtre ⁊ mare gereccan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="77" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="89" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in collo plagietur, ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.1-3"/> inde perpetuam et insanabilem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.2-3"/> contrahat inualitudinem, et tamen uiuat ita contumeliatus, emendetur C solid., si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.3-3"/> non ei sapientum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.4-3"/> rectius et amplius iudicia destinabunt.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_77.lnote.oe.star"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="92" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon oðrum ða geweald<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.9"/> forslea uppe on þam sweoran<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.10"/> ⁊ forwundie<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.11"/> to þam swiðe, þæt he nage þære<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.12"/> geweald, ⁊ hwæðre<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.13"/> lifie<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.14"/> swa gescended<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.15"/>, geselle him mon C scill. to bote, buton him witan ryhtre ⁊ mare gereccan<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Af_77.attnote.fn.16"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="80" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="362" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif mon oðrum ða geweald forslea uppe on þam sweoran ⁊ forwundie to þam swiðe, þæt he nage þære geweald, ⁊ hwæðre lifie swa gescended, geselle him mon C scill to bote, buton him witan ryhtre ⁊ mare gereccan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="89" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.lnote.de.1"/> man einem anderen die ‘Gewalt’ [das Rückgrat?]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_77.lnote.de.2"/> zerschlägt oben am Nacken und [ihn] so sehr verwundet, dass er über<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_77.lnote.de.3"/> sie keine Gewalt hat, und [wenn] er doch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_77.lnote.de.4"/> [weiter] lebt so verschändet, gebe man ihm 100 Schill. zur Busse, es sei denn dass die Richter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_77.lnote.de.5"/> ihm richtiger und mehr zusprechen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_77.lnote.de.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone smashes another’s ‘control’ [the spine?] up at the neck and wounds [him] so badly that he has no control over it, and [if] he nevertheless lives [on] so disfigured, let him be given 100 shillings as compensation, unless the judges award him something more just and more.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="93" ed="#attenborough"/>If one man damages the tendons<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_77.attnote.n.1"/> in another’s neck, and wounds him so severely that he has no control over them, but [if] nevertheless he continues to live so wounded, 100 shillings shall be given to him as compensation, unless the councillors<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_77.attnote.n.2"/> award him a juster and a greater sum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="363" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone injures the power up on the neck, and wounds it so greatly, that he does not have power, and nonetheless lives thus afflicted, let him be paid 100 shillings as compensation, unless the witan adjudge more by law.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">up on þæm sweore <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">up on þæm sweore Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dige to ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dige to ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">ðær</hi> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ðær</hi> Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">ðeah</hi> hwæþere lifige s. gescende, gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ðeah</hi> hwæþere lifige s. gescende, gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hund <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hund Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rihtre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rihtre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> uppe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to uppe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> -ðere</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -ðere</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">88</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">89</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">89</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">insab. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">insab. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">89</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nisi sap. ei <hi rend="italic">Lond Hn</hi> 93, 37</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nisi sap. ei Lond Hn 93, 37</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">89</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. et a. sap. <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. et a. sap. Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">89</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hoc est ut reddantur afflictiones liberorum per plenum, seruorum autem per dimidium <hi rend="italic">fügt zu THkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hoc est ut reddantur afflictiones liberorum per plenum, seruorum autem per dimidium added by THkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Lähmung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Lähmung</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Plural <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> ward von Q nicht, von Inst. ‘Sehnen und Adern’ übersetzt. In letzterem Sinne ist es sonst nicht nachgewiesen. Die Wbb. Toller’s und Sweet’s geben ‘Halssehnen’ bzw. ‘Halsmuskeln’ ohne Beleg. Wahrscheinlich dasselbe Wort ist <hi rend="italic">wælt</hi> in Abt 68. Nicht ‘Kraft’ allgemein kann hier gemeint sein, obwohl das Wort mit dem ‘Gewalt’ bedeutenden <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> identisch scheint. Gar zu schülerhaft wäre ja der Satz: ‘Wenn einer die Kraft so zerschlägt, dass er deren keine Gewalt habe’. Vielmehr muss Af meinen einen zerschlagbaren Körperteil am Halse, dessen Verwundung, auch wenn nicht tödlich, dauerndes schweres Siechtum (wie aus Bussenhöhe folgt) hervorbringt. Auch kann <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> einen anderen ganz bestimmten Körperteil bedeuten: ‘inguen, Schamglied’; Thöne 53. Wahrscheinlich, nach E. Sievers (<hi rend="italic">o.</hi> Af 75²), meint Af Halsmuskeln längs der Wirbelsäule oder, davon nicht scharf geschieden, ‘Rückgrat’. Letzteres scheint mir das Gemeinte nach Friesischem Recht; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Hals 1a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The plural <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> was not translated by Q, and was rendered by Inst. as ‘sinews and veins’. In the latter sense it is not attested elsewhere. Toller’s and Sweet’s dictionaries give ‘neck sinews’ and ‘neck muscles’ respectively, without evidence. Probably the same word is <hi rend="italic">wælt</hi> in Abt 68. ‘Strength’ in general cannot be meant here, although the word seems identical with <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> meaning ‘power’. The sentence ‘If someone so smashes the strength that he has no power of it’ would indeed be all too schoolboyish. Rather, Af must mean a part of the body at the neck that can be smashed, the wounding of which, even if not fatal, produces lasting serious infirmity (as follows from the amount of the compensation). <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> can also denote another quite definite part of the body: ‘inguen, privy member’; Thöne 53. Probably, according to E. Sievers (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> Af 75²), Af means the neck muscles along the spine or, not sharply distinguished from them, the ‘backbone’. The latter seems to me to be what is meant, judging by Frisian law; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Hals 1a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘dort’ B</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘there’ B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B modernises</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘Witan’, sondern ‘Gerichtsobere’; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Af El 21¹⁰</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘witan’, but ‘heads of the court’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Af El 21¹⁰</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_77.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über den Zusatz in Q spät. Rez., dass <hi rend="italic">servi,</hi> d. h. wohl für Mitte des 12. Jhs. ‘Villane’, halbe Wundbusse erhalten sollen, <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> unfrei 7f. 20b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the addition in the later recension of Q, that <hi rend="italic">servi,</hi> i.e. probably, for the middle of the 12th cent., ‘villeins’, are to receive half the compensation for wounds, <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> unfrei 7f. 20b</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>geweald</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gewald</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>sweoran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sweore</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>forwundie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">forwundige</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>þære</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þær</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">ðæra</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>hwæðre</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðeah hwæðere</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>lifie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">lifige</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">libbe</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>gescended</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gescend</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">gescynded</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><label>gereccan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">buton him witon mare gereccan ⁊ ryhtre</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ða geweald</hi> can hardly be used in the abstract sense of <hi rend="italic">geweald</hi> (‘power,’ ‘strength,’ ‘efficiency’). Liebermann compares the word to <hi rend="italic">wælt</hi> in Abt. cap. 68; he suggests the reference here is to the spine.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_77.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the judges of the court in which the case is tried. Some of the MSS of Quadr. add at the end of this cap., <hi rend="italic">hoc est, ut reddantur afflictiones liberorum per plenum, seruorum autem per dimidium.</hi></seg></note>
